            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42010",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gnutls: gnutls: Authentication Bypass via NUL Character in Username"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in gnutls. Servers configured with RSA-PSK (Rivest–Shamir–Adleman – Pre-Shared Key) wrongfully matched usernames containing a NUL character with truncated usernames. A remote attacker could exploit this by sending a specially crafted username, leading to an authentication bypass. This vulnerability allows an attacker to gain unauthorized access by circumventing the authentication process."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42010",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42010\nSeverity: CRITICAL\nPackage: libgnutls30\nFixed Version: 3.7.9-2+deb12u7\nLink: [CVE-2026-42010](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42010)\nA flaw was found in gnutls. Servers configured with RSA-PSK (Rivest–Shamir–Adleman – Pre-Shared Key) wrongfully matched usernames containing a NUL character with truncated usernames. A remote attacker could exploit this by sending a specially crafted username, leading to an authentication bypass. This vulnerability allows an attacker to gain unauthorized access by circumventing the authentication process.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42010**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|CRITICAL|libgnutls30|3.7.9-2+deb12u7|[CVE-2026-42010](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-42010)|\n\nA flaw was found in gnutls. Servers configured with RSA-PSK (Rivest–Shamir–Adleman – Pre-Shared Key) wrongfully matched usernames containing a NUL character with truncated usernames. A remote attacker could exploit this by sending a specially crafted username, leading to an authentication bypass. This vulnerability allows an attacker to gain unauthorized access by circumventing the authentication process."
