            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-3833",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "gnutls: GnuTLS: Policy bypass due to case-sensitive nameConstraints comparison"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in gnutls. This vulnerability occurs because gnutls performs case-sensitive comparisons of `nameConstraints` labels, specifically for `dNSName` (DNS) or `rfc822Name` (email) constraints within `excludedSubtrees` or `permittedSubtrees`. A remote attacker can exploit this by crafting a leaf certificate with casing differences in the Subject Alternative Name (SAN), leading to a policy bypass where a certificate that should be rejected is instead accepted. This could result in unauthorized access or information disclosure."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3833",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-3833\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: libgnutls30\nFixed Version: 3.7.9-2+deb12u7\nLink: [CVE-2026-3833](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3833)\nA flaw was found in gnutls. This vulnerability occurs because gnutls performs case-sensitive comparisons of `nameConstraints` labels, specifically for `dNSName` (DNS) or `rfc822Name` (email) constraints within `excludedSubtrees` or `permittedSubtrees`. A remote attacker can exploit this by crafting a leaf certificate with casing differences in the Subject Alternative Name (SAN), leading to a policy bypass where a certificate that should be rejected is instead accepted. This could result in unauthorized access or information disclosure.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-3833**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|libgnutls30|3.7.9-2+deb12u7|[CVE-2026-3833](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3833)|\n\nA flaw was found in gnutls. This vulnerability occurs because gnutls performs case-sensitive comparisons of `nameConstraints` labels, specifically for `dNSName` (DNS) or `rfc822Name` (email) constraints within `excludedSubtrees` or `permittedSubtrees`. A remote attacker can exploit this by crafting a leaf certificate with casing differences in the Subject Alternative Name (SAN), leading to a policy bypass where a certificate that should be rejected is instead accepted. This could result in unauthorized access or information disclosure."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.4",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
